ision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B1", "label": "Inflammatory Bowel Disease", "posterior": 0.253, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 0, "disconfirming": 0, "last_disconfirming_digest": ""}, "action_intents": [], "considered_alternatives": ["B2", "B4", "B5"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=80%, source=both]\n\nInflammatory Bowel Disease vs Cystic Fibrosis / Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, abnormal intestine morphology, anal fissures, anemia, blood in stool\n  Favours second: abdominal situs inversus, abnormal atrial arrangement, abnormal axonemal organization of respiratory motile cilia, abnormal central microtubular pair morphology of respiratory motile cilia, abnormal ciliary motility\n\nInflammatory Bowel Disease vs Inherited Immunodeficiency:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, abnormal intestine morphology, anal fissures, anemia, blood in stool\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nInflammatory Bowel Disease vs Congenital Cardiac Anomalies with Secondary Pulmonary Hypertension:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, abnormal intestine morphology, anal fissures, anemia, autosomal dominant inheritance\n  Favours second: dyspnea on exertion, edema of lower extremities, exertional anginal pain, hemoptysis, hepatomegaly\n\nCystic Fibrosis / Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia vs Inherited Immunodeficiency:\n  Favours first:  abdominal situs inversus, abnormal atrial arrangement, abnormal axonemal organization of respiratory motile cilia, abnormal central microtubular pair morphology of respiratory motile cilia, abnormal ciliary motility\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nCystic Fibrosis / Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia vs Congenital Cardiac Anomalies with Secondary Pulmonary Hypertension:\n  Favours first:  abdominal situs inversus, abnormal atrial arrangement, abnormal axonemal organization of respiratory motile cilia, abnormal central microtubular pair morphology of respiratory motile cilia, abnormal ciliary motility\n  Favours second: dyspnea on exertion, edema of lower extremities, exertional anginal pain, fatigue, hemoptysis\n\nInherited Immunodeficiency vs Congenital Cardiac Anomalies with Secondary Pulmonary Hypertension:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: dyspnea on exertion, edema of lower extremities, exertional anginal pain, fatigue, hemoptysis\n\nNOT typically seen in Cystic Fibrosis / Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia: abnormal axonemal organization of respiratory motile cilia, abnormal sweat electrolytes, decreased fertility, heterotaxy\n\nNOT typically seen in Inherited Immunodeficiency: abnormal b cell morphology, abnormal lymphocyte morphology, abnormal lymphocyte physiology, abnormal natural killer cell morphology, hemophagocytosis\n\nRelated to Inflammatory Bowel Disease: cap polyposis, chronic granulomatous disease, colitis (disease)\n\nRelated to Cystic Fibrosis / Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia: ciliary discoordination due to random ciliary orientation, ciliary dyskinesia with defective radial spokes, ciliary dyskinesia with excessively long cilia\n\nRelated to Inherited Immunodeficiency: activated pi3k-delta syndrome, agammaglobulinemia, autoimmune enteropathy and endocrinopathy - susceptibility to chronic infections syndrome\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 10-year-old girl is admitted to the medical floor for a respiratory infection → recurrent respiratory infections → Cystic Fibrosis / Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia\n  A 10-year-old girl is admitted to the medical floor for a respiratory infection → recurrent sinopulmonary infections → Cystic Fibrosis / Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia\n  A 10-year-old girl is admitted to the medical floor for a respiratory infection → respiratory tract infection → Cystic Fibrosis / Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia"}
